        "title": "Leatherworking: Tanning, Tooling, and Craft - Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Leather is animal skin structurally transformed by tanning — a chemical process that stabilizes collagen proteins against decay, water, and mechanical stress. The craft of leatherworking spans everything from high-end saddlery and bookbinding to garment construction and fine goods. The tanning method used determines almost everything about what the leather can do."
